IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`
IMPORT `coa-proc-scheme-of-arrangement`

-- coa-proc-scheme-of-arrangement-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-scheme-of-arrangement.l4 (Companies Act 2006, Part 26, ss 895 to 901).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- The module adds no Boolean helper, so this file has no #ASSERT: the gates are the existing functions of coa20-part26.l4, which its own tests cover.
-- Day 0 is the day named in the TIMELINE line of the rule under test. Where the Act gives no time, no clock runs and an unexercised rule stays open (RESIDUAL).

§ `Tests for the scheme of arrangement procedure`

§§ `Traces: s 896, the court orders a meeting`

-- s 896(1): the company applies and the court orders the meeting.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 896(1) the court's power to order a meeting` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the court` DOES `s 896(1) the court orders a meeting to be summoned` AT 3

-- s 896(1): the application is made and the court has not ordered the meeting; the Act gives no time, so the power stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 896(1) the court's power to order a meeting` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 896(1): no application has been made, so the court has no power to order a meeting.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 896(1) the court's power to order a meeting` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 896(2)(c): the applicant is the liquidator and the company is not being wound up, so he may not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 896(1) the court's power to order a meeting` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 897(1), the statement with the notice`

-- s 897(1)(a): a notice sent to a creditor or member goes with the statement.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(1) the company's duty to send the statement with the notice or make it available` TRUE `s 897(1) sent to a creditor or member` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(1)(a) the company sends the notice summoning the meeting accompanied by the statement` AT 4

-- s 897(1)(b)(i): a notice by advertisement includes the statement.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(1) the company's duty to send the statement with the notice or make it available` TRUE `s 897(1) given by advertisement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(1)(b)(i) the company includes the statement in the advertisement` AT 4

-- s 897(1)(b)(ii): a notice by advertisement states where and how copies may be obtained.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(1) the company's duty to send the statement with the notice or make it available` TRUE `s 897(1) given by advertisement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(1)(b)(ii) the company states in the advertisement where and how copies of the statement may be obtained` AT 4

-- s 897(1)(b): the advertisement does neither; the Act gives no time, so the duty stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 897(1) the company's duty to send the statement with the notice or make it available` TRUE `s 897(1) given by advertisement` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 897(1): no meeting is summoned under section 896, so no statement is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(1) the company's duty to send the statement with the notice or make it available` FALSE `s 897(1) sent to a creditor or member` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 897(4), a copy of the statement free of charge`

-- s 897(4): a creditor applies in the manner the advertisement indicates and the company provides the copy.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(4) the company's duty to provide a copy of the statement free of charge` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting` DOES `s 897(4) the creditor or member applies for a copy of the statement` AT 2
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(4) the company provides the copy of the statement free of charge` AT 5

-- s 897(4): the creditor has applied and the company has not provided the copy; the Act gives no time, so the duty stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 897(4) the company's duty to provide a copy of the statement free of charge` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting` DOES `s 897(4) the creditor or member applies for a copy of the statement` AT 2
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 897(4): the advertisement does not state that copies can be obtained, so no entitlement arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(4) the company's duty to provide a copy of the statement free of charge` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 897(5) to (7), the offence`

-- s 897(5): the company makes default and the officer is in default, both on day 6.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(5) the company makes default in complying with a requirement of section 897` AT 6
    PARTY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 897(5) the officer is in default in the company's default` AT 6

-- s 897(5)(a): the company makes default and nothing is said of the officer.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(5) the company makes default in complying with a requirement of section 897` AT 6

-- s 897(5)(b): the company shows the s 897(7) defence, so the company is not guilty; the officer is in default (s 1121) and shows no defence, so the officer is.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 897(5) the officer is in default in the company's default` AT 6

-- s 897(5)(b): the company shows the defence and the officer is not in default (s 1121), so neither is guilty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 897(5) the officer is in default in the company's default` AT 6

-- s 897(7): the company and the officer each show the defence, so neither is guilty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 897(5) the officer is in default in the company's default` AT 6

-- s 897(7): the company makes default and shows the defence, and the officer is not in default, so no one is guilty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 897(5) the company makes default in complying with a requirement of section 897` AT 6

-- s 897(5): no default yet; both prohibitions stay open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 898, the duty of directors and trustees`

-- s 898(1): a director gives the company notice of a matter relating to himself that s 897 needs.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 898(1) the duty of a director or trustee to give the company notice` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` DOES `s 898(1) the director or trustee gives the company notice of the matters relating to himself` AT 3

-- s 898(1): the director has not given notice; the Act gives no time, so the duty stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 898(1) the duty of a director or trustee to give the company notice` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 898(1): the person is not a director or trustee, so no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 898(1) the duty of a director or trustee to give the company notice` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 898(2): a director makes default in complying with section 898.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 898(2) the director's or trustee's duty not to make default` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` DOES `s 898(2) the director or trustee makes default in complying with section 898` AT 5

-- s 898(2): the person is not a director or trustee, so there is no default of this section.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 898(2) the director's or trustee's duty not to make default` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 899, the court sanctions`

-- The numbers below are, in order: the number present and voting, the number who agree, the value present and voting, the value who agree.
-- s 899(1): 8 of 10 in number agree, representing 80 of 100 in value, the company applies: the court sanctions.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 8 100 80 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the court` DOES `s 899(1) the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement` AT 4

-- s 899(1): the majority is shown and the court has not sanctioned; the Act gives no time, so the power stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 8 100 80 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 899(1): 6 of 10 in number agree, representing exactly 75 of 100 in value: exactly 75% in value is enough, and the power is open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 6 100 75 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 899(1): 74 of 100 in value is short of 75%, so the court has no power to sanction.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 8 100 74 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 899(1): 5 of 10 in number is half and not a majority in number, so the court has no power to sanction.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 5 100 80 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 899A(5): the arrangement includes provision for a relevant creditor who has not agreed, so the court may not sanction.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 8 100 80 (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 899(2): the applicant is a person the subsection does not list, so the gate is closed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` `s 896(2) any other person` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 8 100 80 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 899(4), the delivery of the sanctioning order`

-- s 899(4): the court has sanctioned and the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(4) the company's delivery of a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 899(4) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 20

-- s 899(4): no sanction under section 899, so nothing is delivered under this subsection.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 899(4) the company's delivery of a copy of the order to the registrar` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 900(6), the seven days`

-- The inputs are, in order: an application is made under section 899; the compromise is proposed for a reconstruction or amalgamation;
-- under the scheme property or an undertaking is transferred to another company; an order is made under section 900.
-- s 900(6): the copy is delivered on day 3, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 3

-- s 900(6): the copy is delivered on day 7, the seventh day after the order, the last day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 7

-- s 900(6): the copy is delivered on day 8, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 8

-- s 900(6): nothing is delivered and the seven days pass.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)

-- s 900(1): the compromise is not for a reconstruction or amalgamation, so s 900 does not apply and no seven days run.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 900(7), the offence of the company and of every officer in default`

-- The last input is whether the officer is in default (s 1121).
-- s 900(7): the officer is in default and the copy is delivered on day 8, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 900(7) the company and every officer in default` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 8

-- s 900(7): the officer is in default and the copy is delivered on day 7, the last day: no default, so no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 900(7) the company and every officer in default` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 7

-- s 900(7)(a): the officer is not in default (s 1121) and nothing is delivered by day 8: the company alone commits the offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 900(7) the company and every officer in default` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)

§§ `Traces: s 901(2), the amended articles go with the copy of the order`

-- The inputs are, in order: the order is an order under section 899; the order is an order under section 900 that alters the constitution;
-- the order amends the articles or a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement.
-- s 901(2): the amended articles are delivered with the copy, on the day of delivery.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 901(2) the company's duty to deliver the amended articles with the copy of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 901(2) the company delivers the amended articles, resolution or agreement with the copy of the order` AT 0

-- s 901(2): the copy is delivered and the amended articles are not delivered with it.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 901(2) the company's duty to deliver the amended articles with the copy of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1)

-- s 901(2): the order does not amend the articles or a Chapter 3 resolution or agreement, so nothing need accompany the copy.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 901(2) the company's duty to deliver the amended articles with the copy of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

§§ `Traces: s 901(3), each copy of the articles goes with a copy of the order`

-- The inputs are, in order: the order is an order under section 899; the order is an order under section 900 that alters the constitution;
-- the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
-- s 901(3): the company issues a copy of the articles without a copy of the order.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 901(3) the company's duty to accompany each copy of the articles with a copy of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 901(3) the company issues a copy of the articles unaccompanied by a copy of the order` AT 9

-- s 901(3): no unaccompanied copy has been issued; the prohibition stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 901(3) the company's duty to accompany each copy of the articles with a copy of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 901(3): the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment, so a copy need not carry the order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 901(3) the company's duty to accompany each copy of the articles with a copy of the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 895-901 the company` DOES `s 901(3) the company issues a copy of the articles unaccompanied by a copy of the order` AT 9

-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
-- No trace in this file differs in class (FULFILLED, BREACH, RESIDUAL) between the unstable build (a50cbd0, 25 November 2026) and main (112):
-- all 47 traces match their EXPECT on both. The Result block prints differently on main in four traces, all with the same class on both:
--   * the `s 897(5)` trace in which the company makes default and the officer is in default on day 6, and the `s 900(7)` trace in which the copy is delivered
--     on day 8 with the officer in default (each a RAND of two breaches): unstable prints both breaches (the company's and the officer's); main prints only the
--     company's. The class is BREACH on both.
--   * the `s 897(5)` trace with no default yet and the `s 901(3)` trace with no unaccompanied copy yet: unstable prints the open prohibition's LEST with its
--     BREACH in parentheses, main without. The class is RESIDUAL on both.
